<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
"-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
"qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>

<overview>
	<p>
		Websites that rely on cookie-based authentication may be vulnerable to cross-site
		request forgery (CSRF). A state-changing request should include a secret token so
		the request can't be forged by an attacker. Otherwise, unwanted requests can be
		submitted on behalf of a user who visits a malicious website.
	</p>
	<p>
		This query extends the standard <code>js/missing-token-validation</code> query. A
		state-changing route is also considered to rely on cookies when it is guarded by an
		earlier middleware that reads cookie or session state, such as a global session
		authentication check (including middleware wrapped with <code>express-unless</code>).
		Sessions stored by the <code>client-sessions</code> package are also recognized.
	</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
	<p>
		Use a middleware package such as <code>csurf</code> or <code>lusca.csrf</code> to protect
		against CSRF attacks, and register it <em>before</em> the route handlers it should protect.
		Express runs middleware in registration order, so CSRF middleware mounted after a route
		never runs for that route.
	</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
	<p>
		In the example below, every route is authenticated by a session check, but the CSRF
		middleware is only registered after the <code>/transfer</code> route:
	</p>

	<sample src="examples/MissingCsrfMiddlewareBad.js"/>

	<p>
		An attacker can submit a cross-origin POST request to <code>/transfer</code> while the
		victim is logged in. Registering the CSRF middleware before the routes fixes the problem:
	</p>

	<sample src="examples/MissingCsrfMiddlewareGood.js"/>
</example>

<references>
	<li>OWASP: <a href="https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/csrf">Cross Site Request Forgery (CSRF)</a></li>
	<li>Common Weakness Enumeration: <a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/352.html">CWE-352</a></li>
	<li>Express: <a href="https://expressjs.com/en/guide/using-middleware.html">Using middleware</a></li>
</references>
</qhelp>
